What is adapted (the project is a prompt-based skill; its ideas are
reimplemented here, not copied):
- the media inventory and its verification (media_inventory.py,
  verify_inventory.py) -> cutgrammar/inventory.py, inventory.py; the
  approach is kept (read-only, sha256, display orientation, missing /
  changed / unexpected), the code is rewritten on cutgrammar.media.probe;
- evidence levels bounded by how footage was read (metadata / still /
  motion / audio; unverified is "pending", never "done") ->
  cutgrammar/evidence.py, grammar.gate, reject.NEEDS;
- the preference state machine (an edit is a candidate; five sortings;
  only an explicit "keep this" with scope and counter-example becomes a
  long-term rule; changes are logged, never silently overwritten) ->
  web/backend/preferences.py;
- the semantic-anchor method, narrowed to what can be computed (the voice
  sets the time; what is said picks the footage; labels recall but never
  rank; unmatched lines are listed gaps, never covered; the same source is
  not used back to back; timing states text_only / estimated, never locked
  without watching) -> web/backend/voiceover.py.
Its templates, reference documents and worked example are not included.
